Prefer **`SCR_`** types over thinner native/`GameCode` types — they have the methods mods actually need. Match inheritance exactly (`ScriptComponent` vs `GameComponent` vs `SCR_BaseGameModeComponent`). Match lifecycle names exactly (`OnPostInit` vs `EOnInit` vs `OnGameModeStart`).

## Language

- **No ternary** (`?:`). Use `if / else`. Enforce does not have it.
- **Every `new` lives in a `ref`** — member (`protected ref T m_x;`), local (`ref T x = new T();`), or `ref array<ref T>`. Missing `ref` on a `Managed` instance → ARC drops it → `NULL pointer` later (often in `AddChild` or the next frame). Vanilla `RemoveStaticMarker` on a server marker drops the manager `ref` then calls `GetMarkerID()` again — a non-`ref` holder NPEs on that second access. Keep a `ref` across the call. Evidence: `SCR_MapMarkerManagerComponent.c:272-287`; `runtime:` admin Complete Zone during seize (`IA_DynamicSiteInstance.RemoveMapMarker`).
- **`autoptr` is legacy.** Bohemia formatter: remove it on ordinary locals, or replace with `ref` on member arrays. New code uses `ref`.
- **No `auto`.** Name the type.
- **Script methods are capped at 16 arguments.** `Maximum arguments count 16 exceeded` fails the Game module. Pack extras into a string or bitmask. RPCs are a tighter cap of **8**. Evidence: `compiler: IA_MissionInitializer.c` `PackAdminConfig`.
- **`CallLater` does not apply default parameter values.** The queued call must pass every argument the method declares, or it is `Not enough parameters, expected N got M`. Direct calls still use defaults. Evidence: `runtime:` `_SpawnSingleAiGroupAndAddToArea` after three hold-post args were added (`IA_AreaInstance.c` mortar pit gunners/guards).
- **`System.GetTickCount()` is ms since game start; `GetUnixTime()` is wall-clock seconds.** `IA_AiGroup` stores danger as Unix. `tickNow - dangerUnix < windowMs` is a huge negative, so the `< window` test is always true. Compare Unix to Unix (or convert). Evidence: `core/.../System.c` GetTickCount; `IA_AI_Group.c` `m_lastDangerEventTime = System.GetUnixTime()`; `runtime:` Enhanced Defense PREPARE HUD stuck at 2:15/2:16.
- **`EAISkill` only changes aim-error sigma.** `NONE/NOOB/ROOKIE/REGULAR/VETERAN/EXPERT/CYLON` — `CYLON` (100) returns zero offset and is above `EXPERT` (80). It does not change reaction time or fire rate. Those use `SetPerceptionFactor` / `SetFireRateCoef`. `SetFireRateCoef(coef, persistent: true)` keeps group fire-rate orders from overwriting a soldier-specific value. Evidence: `Game/AI/Components/SCR_AICombatComponent.c`; `Game/AI/ScriptedNodes/Aiming/SCR_AIGetAimErrorOffset.c`; `SCR_AIGetFireTimes.c`.
- **`SCR_AICombatComponent` lives on the controlled character, not the `AIAgent`.** Vanilla always does `agent.GetControlledEntity().FindComponent(SCR_AICombatComponent)`. `agent.FindComponent(...)` is usually null. `EOnInit` copies `m_eAISkillDefault` onto the live skill, so `SetAISkill` before that init is overwritten back to the prefab default (`Character_Base` empty combat block is Regular / `"50"`). Apply after init or `CallLater`. Evidence: `SCR_ScenarioFrameworkSlotAI.c:364-368`; `SCR_AICombatComponent.c` `EOnInit`; `Character_Base.et`.
- **`Class` is the super-root. `Managed` is GC'd.** Downcast with `T.Cast(obj)`, then null-check. `IsInherited(typename)`. An `IEntity` cannot be passed implicitly to an `AIWaypoint` argument; preserve the waypoint subtype in stored members or explicitly cast. Evidence: `compiler: IA_AI_Group.c:5981` `Unsafe down-casting`; typing the stored artillery waypoint restored the Game module and cleared the cascading vanilla missing-class errors (Workbench `logs_2026-09-08_19-42-41`).
- **`null` is not an enum value.** Enums are ints. `ShouldDefer(null, waypoint)` when the first arg is `IA_AiOrder` is `Cannot convert 'Class' to 'int'`. Split the overload or pass a real enum. Evidence: `compiler: IA_AI_Group.c` `ShouldDeferForTypedWaypointTree`.
- **`pointer` types cannot be class members.** They are plain C++ pointers with no weak refs and no GC (`Types.c`). `Physics` is `NativeComponent : pointer`, so `protected Physics m_Physics` is `Pointer type 'Physics' can only be used with local variables` and can block the Game script module. Fetch a local with `owner.GetPhysics()`; cache `IEntity` if you need the owner. `global_pointer` is the subtype `Types.c` marks "Safe to store outside local scope". Evidence: `compiler: MHJ_CanopyFlight.c`; `Physics.c`, `NativeComponent.c`, `Types.c`.
- **Overrides must match inherited parameter names too.** Renaming the parameter of `MeasureHierarchy` in a derived Workbench probe failed with `name differs from prototype`; use the inherited name or a differently named helper. Evidence: `compiler: IA_BaseCompositionProbe.c`, Workbench log `logs_2026-09-06_00-31-39`.
- **`int` arithmetic wraps like C int32.** Negative multiplier literals, such as `h * -1640531535`, overflow and wrap exactly as in C, so a murmur3-style finaliser matches a Python int32 emulation. Mask right shifts (`(h >> 15) & 131071`) so results do not depend on sign extension. Evidence: `IA_BaseDesignLibrary.Mix`; `IA_HeadquartersDesignTest` failures=0 (`logs_2026-09-25_23-06-13`).
- **Array indexed reads are temporary values for increment operators.** `values[index]++` fails with `Operator '++' is not supported on temporary values`; write `values[index] = values[index] + 1`. Evidence: `compiler: IA_BaseDesignTest.c`, Workbench log `logs_2026-09-06_01-14-59`.
- **Array `Remove` / `RemoveItem` swap the last element into the removed slot.** FIFO and round-robin queues must use `RemoveOrdered` / `RemoveItemOrdered` to retain order and prevent starvation. Evidence: `Core/proto/Types.c:258-269,304-315` (source inspection).
- **Locals are function-scoped, not block-scoped.** A later `if` cannot redeclare a name already used above in the same method; that is `Multiple declaration of variable`. Reuse the existing local or pick a new name. Evidence: `compiler: IA_CompositionGunBuilder.c:150` `parent` / `access`.
- **A subclass cannot redeclare a member or method name its base classes already use.** A field named like an inherited one is `Multiple declaration of variable`, and a method with an inherited name and no `override` (a new `static` included) is `Multiple declaration of function`; the Game module will not compile. Check the whole chain, engine classes included, or pick a more specific name. Evidence: `compiler: IA_HeliPaintTile.c` `m_sName` (public on `MUI_Node`); `IA_HeliPaintMenu.c` static `IsOpen` (`GameLib/generated/Menu/MenuBase.c`).
- **Subclass constructors must match prototype parameter names** for inherited ctor args. `ScriptedCommand` is `protected void ScriptedCommand(BaseAnimPhysComponent pAnimPhysComponent)`. Renaming that first arg (e.g. `animPhysComponent`) is `SCRIPT (E): … name differs from prototype 'pAnimPhysComponent'` and the Game script module will not compile. Extra parameters after the prototype are fine. Evidence: `compiler: MHJ_HaloCommand.c`; `ScriptedCommand.c`; vanilla `SCR_CharacterCommandSwim` / `SCR_CharacterCommandFly`.
- **`notnull` in a signature is a contract**, not a runtime gift. Still validate at trust boundaries.
- **`out` / `inout` / `owned`** are real. `out` = callee writes; `inout` = read then write; `owned` on proto returns = VM must not release the string/array.
- **`proto` / `native` / `volatile`** mark C++ bindings. Do not invent `proto` methods in addon code.
- **`sealed class` cannot be extended.** If you need a hook, find a non-sealed owner or a `modded class` further up.
- **`foreach (T x : container)`** and `foreach (K k, V v : map)` work. Always brace loops. Cache `Count()` — do not call it as the `for` bound every iteration.
- **`Math.RandomInt(min, max)` max is exclusive.** `RandomInt(0, 1)` is always 0. `RandomInt(0, Count() - 1)` with 2 items always returns index 0, so every pick is the first element. Use `RandomInt(0, Count())` and clamp if the result equals Count. Evidence: `core/.../Math/Math.c`; `runtime:` GM-placed AOs stacked every vehicle on one road vertex.
- **`string.Format("%1 …", a)`** and `PrintFormat` accept at most **nine substitution arguments**; split longer reports. Evidence: `Core/generated/Types/string.c:134`, `Core/proto/EnDebug.c:17`. `Print(x, LogLevel.XXX)` — bare `Print()` is a formatter finding. **A `Format` result is lost when it is the left side of a `+` whose right side calls a method that formats too:** `string.Format("a %1 ", n) + Other()` came out as `Other`'s last `Format` result followed by `Other`'s return value. Put the first result in a local before the call. Evidence: `runtime: IA_UplinkMenuProbe` mark `registerServer=0 total=0sync=0 …`, `logs_2026-10-01_21-12-32`.
- **REST and JSON** (`RestCallback` success and error paths, what `GetData()` holds, answer sizes, `JsonLoadContext.ReadValue` into typed rows) moved to `.cursor/rules/enfusion-rest.mdc`. Read it before working on a call to a web service; add new facts there.
- **Chained `+` concatenations can be `Formula too complex`.** Split into sequential `s = s + …` assignments. Evidence: `compiler: IA_Config.c` `PackDefenseExtras`.
- **`vector`** is `<x,y,z>`; index `[0] [1] [2]`. Y is up. `Vector(x,y,z)` constructs. `GetGame().GetWorld().GetSurfaceY(x, z)` is the **terrain mesh only** — rocks, foundations, and buildings are not included. Spawning at that Y clips infantry inside those volumes. Trace down with `TraceFlags.WORLD | ENTS` (or `SCR_WorldTools.FindEmptyTerrainPosition`) from above the sample, keep the hit height, and require standing clearance. Evidence: `Game/Global/SCR_WorldTools.c` `FindEmptyTerrainPosition`; `World.GetSurfaceY`.
- **Colors:** `Color.FromSRGBA(r,g,b,a)` (sRGB bytes) or `Color.FromInt`. Do not `new Color(0.93, …)` with sRGB floats.
- **No lambdas** as a design habit. Use named methods, `func`, or `ScriptInvoker` / `ScriptInvokerBase<>`.
- **One class per file**, file name = class name. Companion `MyThingClass : ScriptComponentClass` stays in the same file as `MyThing`.

```
// BAD — ternary, missing ref, autoptr
int a = flag ? 1 : 0;
MUI_Panel p = new MUI_Panel();

// GOOD
int a;
if (flag)
	a = 1;
else
	a = 0;
ref MUI_Panel p = new MUI_Panel();
```

## Extending the game

Order of preference:

1. **New class** you own (`class IA_Foo : SCR_Bar`) when you control spawn/prefab sites.
2. **Composition** — new `ScriptComponent` on a prefab rather than overriding a huge vanilla class.
3. **`modded class`** only when you must inject into a type you do not own.

```
modded class SCR_SomeClass
{
	override void Method()
	{
		super.Method();
		// additive behavior
	}
}

modded enum ChimeraMenuPreset
{
	MyMenu
}
```

- Always **`super`** unless the method is an intentional full replacement.
- **`modded class` merges** into the original. `super.Method()` calls the original implementation of that same class, not its original parent. Validate exception-prone inputs before delegating; a guard after `super` cannot prevent the original method's exception. Keep overrides tiny. Do not paste GameSources bodies. Evidence: `runtime:` `SCR_AIGetInNearestWaypointParameters` raised `Wrong class of provided Waypoint!` from the modded guard's initial `super` call (`logs_2026-09-08_19-42-41`, 20:03:24).
- **A `modded class` is not a private-field test-access shim.** Placing a merge of a Game class in WorkbenchGame failed `Unknown type`; moving it to Game then broke private-field access in the original class's static factories as well as the shim. Keep tests needing those private internals inside the original class under `#ifdef WORKBENCH`, called by a Workbench plugin. Evidence: compiler `IA_DynamicAIGroupRegression.c`, logs `23-14-30` / `23-15-28`; original-class regression compiled and passed in `23-16-23` (2026-09-08).
- **`modded enum`** adds values. Do not re-list existing values.
- **A `modded class` can override a `static` method and call `super`.** `override static T M(args) { return F(super.M(args)); }` compiles, and every caller of `Original.M` gets the modded result. The editor runs each prefab through `SCR_EditableEntityComponentClass.GetRandomVariant` on the server just before it spawns it (`SCR_PlacingEditorComponent.CreateEntityServer`), so that static is the hook to change what Game Master or build mode spawns; `OnEntityCreatedServer` is not (build mode overrides it without `super`). Evidence: `IA_HeliPaintEditorSpawn.c`; `IA_HeliSkinLiveProbe` mode 4, `logs_2026-10-01_11-36-14`; `SCR_CampaignBuildingPlacingEditorComponent.c:132`. A spawn through the editor interface itself is not yet seen.
- Generated files (`Do not modify, this script is generated`) are bindings. Mod them only when there is no scripted `SCR_` wrapper.

## Components and lifecycle

Scripted components inherit **`ScriptComponent`** (`GenericComponent`). Game-mode extras inherit **`SCR_BaseGameModeComponent`** and must sit on a GameMode entity. **`GameComponent`** is a thinner generated type — do not pick it just because the name sounds right.

Every attachable component needs a companion prefab-data class:

```
[ComponentEditorProps(category: "MyMod/Components", description: "…")]
class MyCompClass : ScriptComponentClass
{
}

class MyComp : ScriptComponent
{
	override void OnPostInit(IEntity owner)
	{
		super.OnPostInit(owner);
		SetEventMask(owner, EntityEvent.INIT);
	}
}
```

- **`SetEventMask` in the constructor does not stick** on the parent entity. Set it in `OnComponentInsert` / `OnPostInit`. Evidence: `GenericComponent.c`.
- Events fire only if the mask bit is set: `EOnInit` needs `EntityEvent.INIT`, `EOnFrame` needs `FRAME`, etc.
- **`OnPostInit`** = all components on that entity are in. **`EOnInit`** = `EV_INIT` registered. **`OnGameModeStart`** is a game-mode callback, not a component init alias.
- Avoid **`EOnFrame` / `EOnFixedFrame`** unless nothing else works. Prefer events, timers, invokers. Unsubscribe on deactivate/delete.
- Constructors stay cheap. No world queries, no RPC, no spawn in `void MyComp()`.

Cast components: `RplComponent.Cast(owner.FindComponent(RplComponent))`. Cache the pointer. Null-check every time at a trust boundary.

## Replication

Gameplay is **server-authoritative**. Guard world mutation with `Replication.IsServer()` or `RplComponent.IsMaster()`. `IsProxy()` means this machine is not authority for that entity.

- Client: prediction, FX, UI. Validate every client-originating request on the server.
- **Use `PlayerManager.GetPlayerCount()` for the live connected-player total.** `GetPlayers(out ids)` returns that connected set when IDs are needed; `GetAllPlayers(out ids)` also includes disconnected players. Do not reuse gameplay scaling helpers that count controlled pawns or substitute a baseline during mission setup for population gates. Evidence: `Game/generated/Network/PlayerManager.c`; vanilla deploy/welcome UI; `IA_Game.GetPlayerCount`.
- **The engine has three script reads for the running server's name, and all three are empty in Workbench.** `GetGame().GetServerInfo()` is null, `GetGame().GetBackendApi().GetRunningDSConfig(new SCR_DSConfig())` is false, and `ServerLobbyApi.IsEnabled()` is false with `ServerLobbyApi.GetServerConfig()` null, in edit and in play mode; all compile in the Game module. Null-check each and keep a fallback. `DSSession.Name()` is obsolete and returns `""`. What they return on a dedicated server is not yet seen: vanilla reads `GetServerInfo().GetName()` on clients only (`SCR_StatsPanel_ServerName.c`) and `GetRunningDSConfig` on the authority (`SCR_ReconnectComponent.c:51`), and no vanilla script calls `ServerLobbyApi`. Evidence: `IA_ServerNameProbe`, `logs_2026-10-01_19-24-16`.
- **`modded class` on a snapshot-serialized type drops Encode/Decode.** `SCR_MapMarkerBase` is an RPC payload (`RPC_DoAddStaticMarker` / `RPC_AskAddStaticMarker`). It ships static `Extract` / `Inject` / `Encode` / `Decode` / `SnapCompare` / `PropCompare`. A merge of that class without those methods is `Type cannot be replicated` and the Game module will not compile. Hook pin widgets from `SCR_MapMarkersUI` (or another non-snapshot owner); do not mod the payload type. Evidence: `compiler: MHJ_MapMarkerBase.c`; `SCR_MapMarkerBase.c`; `SCR_MapMarkerManagerComponent.c`.
- RPCs: `[RplRpc(RplChannel.Reliable, RplRcver.Server)]` (or `Broadcast` / owner). Invoke with `Rpc(RpcAsk_Foo, args)` — **same name**, max **8** parameters (`GenericComponent.Rpc`).
- Replicated properties: `[RplProp(onRplName: "OnChanged")]`. Keep payloads small; debounce where possible.
- `RplLoad` / `RplSave` on `ScriptComponent` are the JIP path. If a late joiner must see state, put it here or on an `RplProp`.
- Do not use `Replication.FindItem` after an entity's RplId is gone (vanilla comments call this out on task removal).
- **`RplCreationError: Number of items mismatch`** on join is fatal: client kick `group=1 REPLICATION reason=1 SYSTEM_FAILURE`. expected=N is the authority layout, created=M is the local prefab. Do not GUID-override vanilla replicated prefabs to add/remove `RplComponent` children; put I&A-only Rpl/destruction on the composition instance. Evidence: `runtime: TransmitterTower_01.xob expected=4 created=5` (`ScriptedRadioComponent` extra on client), KickDialogs `REPLICATION_SYSTEM_FAILURE`.
- **`RplError.TIMEOUT`** is a kick (`group=REPLICATION`). Hung insertion after `GiveExt`, or deleting the node while a proxy is still inserting / `IsGettingIn`, surfaces as a timeout around land if freefall continues during the board wait. Evidence: `RplError.c`; `runtime: user report` freefall never became canopy then replication timeout on landing.
- **`NwkMovementComponent` lives on `Vehicle_Base`, not `Vehicle_Cargo_Base` / `Vehicle_Part_Base`.** Adding it to a cargo GenericEntity is an extra movement replication channel the working parachute cargo prefab does not have. Script-moved cargo uses `RplComponent.ForceNodeMovement` (dynamic sim) plus an authority pose snapshot. Evidence: `Vehicle_Base.et`, `Vehicle_Cargo_Base.et`, `RplComponent.c`.
- **Cargo replica must apply the authority snapshot origin every packet.** Native rpl does not move cargo (no `NwkMovementComponent`). Velocity-only dead-reckon drifts until it hits the snap threshold (error hugs 10 m, then 40 m after the threshold was raised). 20 ms ping cannot explain 40 m. Apply snapshot origin + velocity; keep replica gravity off. Evidence: `runtime: logs_2026-08-19_19-09-15` `Replica snap error=10.1–12.2`; `logs_2026-08-19_19-32-03` `40.0–41.7` repeating.
- **Cargo `RigidBody` defaults to `SimState Collision`.** That is collision-only; it does not fly. Working deployed parachutes override to `SimState Simulation`. Occupancy should gate input, not the authority flight tick — sleeping physics until `GetOccupant()` matches freezes a seated jumper in midair. Evidence: `Vehicle_Cargo_Base.et`, `DeployedParachuteMK4.et`; `runtime: user report` open then hover.
- **`GiveExt` does not move `RplRole.Authority`.** Owner GetIn/steer RPCs need the player identity; jitter was dual writers (authority transform plus proxy physics), not GiveExt itself. Do not wait for `IsOwner()` before `GetInVehicle` — insertion lags GiveExt; GetIn as soon as `FindItem` resolves and retry on false. Evidence: `RplComponent.GiveExt`; parachute owner resolve GetIn then wait for ownership; `runtime: logs_2026-08-17_22-17-01` dual-sim jitter.
- **A client can only send `RplRcver.Server` RPCs on a node it owns.** On a server-owned entity (`RplComponent.IsOwner()` false on the client) the call is silently dropped — no warning, the server just never sees input. After GiveExt, owner steer can go on the canopy; occupancy can still be detected on authority via `slot.GetOccupant()` if the confirm RPC has not arrived. Evidence: `runtime: [MHJ] Canopy diag … srv=1 turn=0 pitchIn=0` every frame while the client held steer, `rplOwner=0` (`logs_2026-08-17_22-32-57`).
- **`SetYawPitchRoll` / `SetOrigin` on an AI pawn does not give dedicated clients a flight pose.** Replica facing stays spawn/animation, and zeroed physics means origin often does not move every frame, so a local-only mesh cannot infer yaw/pitch/bank from `GetYawPitchRoll` or a 2 cm delta. Broadcast heading/path/bank. Evidence: `runtime:` AI drop chute frozen at cruise pitch on dedicated clients after copying the replica.
- **An unreliable pose RPC can arrive after a reliable remove.** If the pose handler calls Add when the id is missing, local-only FX respawn on a pawn that already landed. Tombstone finished ids and never spawn from the pose channel. Evidence: `runtime:` AI walking with canopy still attached after land.
- **`StartCommand_Vehicle` on the server pawn is not GetIn** on the owning client. Treating `GetCommandVehicle()` as seated lets the server fly the replica away from a still-standing client pawn (duplicate chute, fall graph). Gate aero on `slot.IsOccupied()` / `CompartmentAccessComponent` occupancy. Evidence: same log, `haloCmd=0 jumping=1` then `GetIn ok tries=4`.

## Character input, commands, attachments

- **Never `ResetContext` an `InputManager` context on a tick.** Reset wipes click-filter rising edges, so held analog (move, look) still works while crouch, draw, fire, and stance die. `ActivateContext(name, durationMs)` each frame without Reset is how contexts stay alive — vanilla does that. Evidence: `runtime:` post-landing "movement works, nothing else does" from per-frame `ResetContext` (`logs_2026-08-17_22-45-22`).
- **An addon adds input actions with its own `Configs/System/chimeraInputCommon.conf` holding only the new `Action` and `ActionContext` entries.** It merges with the vanilla file: `ActivateContext` on the new context returned true and `IsContextActive` was true in Workbench play mode. A keybinding-menu row is the same kind of delta in `keyBindingMenu.conf`, under the vanilla category's GUID. Evidence: `IA_HeliPaintMenuProbe`, `logs_2026-10-01_11-16-11`. The action firing from its key and the keybinding row are not yet seen in game.
- **Cargo-seat `ForcedFreeLook 1` is not reliably cleared by GetOut on a server-owned, script-moved vehicle.** On the owner client, controller `forceFL=0` but seat freelook remained `free=1`; GetOut briefly reached `camFL=0 xferAim=0`, then native restored `camFL=1 xferAim=1` by t+1000 with occupancy clean. Set the custom canopy seat `ForcedFreeLook 0`, clear all three controller freelook inputs after GetOut, then cancel transfer-freeaim. Evidence: `runtime: logs_2026-08-18_21-25-48`, owner `[MHJ] LAND`.
- **Inactive vehicle contexts were not the persistent equipment cause.** The owner log had `carCtx=0` and `seatCtx=0` throughout the clean GetOut while equipment remained dead; resetting those contexts did nothing. Do not add speculative context resets. Do not swallow `HandleWeapons` unless a scripted command actually owns the pawn; native Fall plus canopy must leave the default weapon pipeline alone. Evidence: `runtime: logs_2026-08-18_21-25-48`.
- **Working cargo parachutes restore infantry with native `GetOutVehicle_NoDoor` only.** That is `AskOwnerToGetOutFromVehicle(..., ejectOnTheSpot=true)`, then delete ~200 ms later. They never `StartCommand_Move`, never `CMD_Vehicle_EndControl`, never script freelook/contexts, and the seat stays `ForcedFreeLook 1`. MHJ `StartCommand_Move` after a clean GetOut produced `veh=0 move=1` with `wpnCtx=0 free=1 camFL=1 xferAim=1` through t+1000; `SetFreeLook(false)` and `ActivateContext` from `HandleWeapons` did not change that. Evidence: `ArmaReforgerParachutes` `ParachuteComponent.Rpc_ServerExitParachute`; `SCR_CompartmentAccessComponent.GetOutOwner`; `runtime: logs_2026-08-19_16-34-32`.
- **Writing `CharacterInputContext.SetAimingAngles` / `SetHeadingAngle` every frame eats the live mouse delta.** The player's yaw is folded and zeroed before the turn machinery sees it, so the head moves and the body never turns. Any "fold leftover look into heading" recovery is one-shot, never a tick. Same log.
- **A recovery flag whose exit test can be permanently true never exits.** `InputManager.IsContextActive("CharacterFreelookMouseContext")` is true during normal on-foot play, so using it as "freelook is stuck" pinned a landing recovery forever. Test controller state (`IsFreeLookForced`, `IsFreeLookEnabled` without `GetFreeLookInput`) and always bound the window with a countdown. Same log.
- **`CallCommand(BindCommand("CMD_Locomotion_Fall"), -1, 0)` still starts the fall clip; `-1` does not cancel it.** The player graph transitions on `IsCommand(CMD_Locomotion_Fall)` and does not inspect the integer payload, so any call wins the Falling transition. Stop issuing the command; then assert `CMD_Vehicle_StartControl` while the vehicle command is active, because `Locomotion.agf` enters `VehicleAttachment` on `CMD_Vehicle_GetIn` / `CMD_Vehicle_StartControl`. Evidence: `data/anims/workspaces/player/Locomotion.agf`; runtime had `cmd=23 vehCmd=1 seat=1` while still rendering fall.
- **Do not `StartCommand_Vehicle` after `GetInVehicle`.** Working cargo parachutes only call `GetInVehicle`; native GetIn creates `CharacterCommandVehicle`. A script-started vehicle command can occupy and GetOut to `veh=0 move=1` while leaving `wpnCtx=0 free=1 camFL=1 xferAim=1` (equipment dead, survives respawn). Occupancy-gating that call also deadlocks boarding. If native GetIn after a custom `ScriptedCommand` never occupies, the leftover is the scripted command, not a missing Vehicle start. Evidence: `ArmaReforgerParachutes` `TryEnterChute_Owner`; `runtime: logs_2026-08-19_16-41-09` `GetIn accepted and vehicle command started` then land dump with those flags.
- **Do not replace locomotion with a `ScriptedCommand` if the next step is native GetIn.** Working parachutes stay on `CharacterCommandFall` until GetIn creates Vehicle. A pawn-driven `SetOrigin` freefall rubber-bands against character replication; HALO now drives one cargo craft instead (`SetVelocity` + `ForceNodeMovement`). Native Fall is only the GetIn bridge — keep pawn gravity on and reassert Fall until occupied. Native Fall stores jump-altitude height until `Land()` — GetOut then applies delayed `EFallDamageType.LANDING` death with no injuries on touchdown. Consume with `Land(LANDTYPE_NONE, 0)` and ignore fall/collision-defaultHZ damage for a few seconds after exit. Evidence: `runtime: user report` 2026-08-19 walk-at-altitude then soft land then delayed death; `logs_2026-08-19_17-53-27` dual pawn `SetOrigin`; `SCR_CharacterDamageManagerComponent.OnHandleFallDamage`.
- **`GetInVehicle(..., forceTeleport: true)` ignores `doorInfoIndex`.** Pass `-1` like vanilla teleport GetIn. Same-vehicle seat changes are another `GetInVehicle` — no GetOut between slots (`SCR_ChangeComparmentAction`). Evidence: `CompartmentAccessComponent.c`; `SCR_ChangeComparmentAction.c`.
- **`RigidBody ModelGeometry 0` disables model-backed physics.** `GetPhysics()` is null, `EntityEvent.SIMULATE` does not run, and `SetVelocity` / `ForceNodeMovement` never apply — the craft hangs. A working cargo parachute leaves `ModelGeometry` enabled. Hide a mesh with transparent material while retaining its geometry; do not disable model geometry on a simulated cargo entity. Evidence: `runtime: logs_2026-08-19_18-28-17` and retest with VObject retained both hovered, dedicated `DataCollectorDriverModule: Couldn't find the vehicle's physics`; working `DeployedParachuteMK4.et` has no `ModelGeometry 0`.
- **A custom `ScriptedCommand` must fully transition to native Fall/Move *before* calling `GetInVehicle`.** Calling GetIn first and then finishing through `HandleFinishedCommandsDefault` starts native Fall on the accepted request and immediately cancels the entry (`in=0 gettingIn=0 gettingOut=0`). Prefer not using a scripted command at all; if one exists, restore exported world velocity, finish it through vanilla, wait for `GetCommandFall()` / `GetCommandMove()`, then call GetIn. Evidence: `runtime: logs_2026-08-18_22-33-10` GetIn accepted at 22:34:31.341, all compartment states idle at timeout.
- **After `GetInVehicle` returns true, do not reissue GetIn because `IsGettingIn()` is not yet true.** The accepted action can have a pending slot reservation before the public access state surfaces; retrying every 50 ms produces a stream of refusals and prevents a clean handoff. Match vanilla parachute behavior: retry only a false return, and leave a true return alone. Evidence: `runtime: logs_2026-08-18_22-40-27` first GetIn accepted, then every retry refused beginning 101 ms later.
- **Custom commands with global `InputManager` listeners need explicit entity-change cleanup.** Death/entity replacement may not provide a usable normal command handoff; remove action listeners and forced-look overrides from `OnControlledEntityChanged(from, to)` before dropping the old command reference. Evidence: `runtime: logs_2026-08-18_22-33-10` failed canopy started a second scripted fall, death followed, equipment remained unavailable after respawn.
- **`SubhandlerStatesBegin` / `SubhandlerStatesEnd` only run while a scripted command owns the pawn.** GameSources calls them "callback for handling scripted commands from default command handler". Any countdown or recovery ticked there stops the moment your `ScriptedCommand` ends, so flags stay latched for the rest of the character's life. Post-command work belongs on the call queue or in a `Handle*` override, which the pipeline calls every frame. Evidence: `runtime: [MHJ] Canopy land check … suppress=1` still set 400 ms after landing with `veh=0 move=1`, the exact condition the tick clears (`logs_2026-08-17_23-10-52`).
- **Do not call `InterruptVehicleActionQueue` to “finish” a GetOut.** Its generated API comment says it interrupts the get-in/get-out process; calling it immediately after `GetOutVehicle*`, issuing duplicate GetOuts, or manually `RemoveChild`-ing the pawn before `IsGettingOut()` clears bypasses the vehicle-exit cleanup that restores infantry state. Issue one exit, wait until both `IsInCompartment()` and `IsGettingOut()` are false, then recover locomotion. Evidence: `CompartmentAccessComponent.c`; runtime emitted four owner GetOut calls in one frame before leaving controls broken (`logs_2026-08-17_23-21-55`).
- **`SetTransferFreeaimAfterFreelookRequest(true)` asks the controller to retain free aim after freelook.** Do not set it during an on-foot restoration intended to return mouse yaw to body turning; use `false`, clear freelook once, and avoid delayed repeated aim-angle writes. A one-shot clear at GetOut-done does not stick: `camFL`/`xferAim` were 0 at restore and 1 two seconds later, then `free=1 freeMouse=1` at t+5s. `SetFreeLook(false)` itself queues that transfer — cancel it after the disable. A cargo slot `ForcedFreeLook 1` re-applies it after GetOut even when `inComp=0`. Evidence: generated `CharacterInputContext.c`; `runtime: logs_2026-08-18_18-51-35` getout-done vs t+200.
- **`IEntity.GetOrigin()` is parent relative.** A character seated in a compartment is a child of the vehicle, so `GetOrigin()` / `GetTransform()` is the seat offset, not a world pose. `GetOutVehicle_NoDoor` must use `GetWorldTransform` plus `ChimeraCharacter.AimingPosition()` (vanilla `GetOutOwner` in `SCR_CompartmentAccessComponent.c`). Passing seat-local coords as the exit teleport leaves `PhysicsIsLinked` and `IsInVehicle` set.
- **`StartCommand_Move` / `StartCommand_Fall` while still seated aborts GetOut.** The vehicle command is required for compartment exit. Interrupting it leaves `PhysicsIsLinked` (head-only look, weapons blocked). Working parachutes call `AskOwnerToGetOutFromVehicle(EGetOutType.TELEPORT, …)` once, keep cargo `RigidBody` in `Simulation` through GetOut, and delete ~200 ms later with no Fall/Move inject. Evidence: `SCR_CompartmentAccessComponent.c`, `CharacterCamera1stPerson.c`; `ArmaReforgerParachutes` `ParachuteComponent.Rpc_ServerExitParachute`.
- **Individual AI do shoot vehicle occupants.** Group perception skips `PerceivableComponent.IsInCompartment()` so the *group* tracks the vehicle instead (`SCR_AIGroupPerception.c`). Soldiers still attack; in a vehicle they aim `EAimPointType.WEAK` (head). They **never** attack `IsDisarmed()` targets (`TARGET_MAX_DISTANCE_DISARMED = 0` in `SCR_AICombatComponent.c`). `Vehicle_Cargo_Base` has no `SCR_VehiclePerceivableComponent` (`Vehicle_Base` does), so a seated cargo jumper has no vehicle for the group to shoot. HALO also `SetInteractionLayer(0)` during hidden freefall (working MK4 stays `0x4040`); traces then miss the linked pawn so `GetTimeSinceSeen` never updates and the fire tree stays LOOK. Evidence: `Vehicle_Base.et`, `Vehicle_Cargo_Base.et`, `SCR_AIUpdateTargetAttackData.c`.
- **`Locomotion.agf` leaves `VehicleAttachment` only on `CMD_Vehicle_EndControl`.** Enter is `CMD_Vehicle_GetIn` / `CMD_Vehicle_StartControl`. `CharacterCommandVehicle` re-issues StartControl in PreAnim, so a handler `CallCommand(EndControl)` is discarded until `StartCommand_Move` replaces that command. Sitting pose plus no infantry weapons after a canopy GetOut means EndControl never won a frame. After a clean GetOut, `StartCommand_Move` alone went `cmd=23 veh=1` → `cmd=21 move=1` while `stance=0` (sit) stayed. Evidence: `data/data/anims/workspaces/player/Locomotion.agf`; `BaseAnimPhysComponent.c`; `runtime: logs_2026-08-18_18-25-32` leave / land restore / land check.
- **A child entity hand-added to a character (`AddChild`) stops rendering once the compartment re-parents the pawn into a vehicle.** For local-only cosmetics, spawn unparented (`ETransformMode.WORLD`) and drive `SetWorldTransform` + `Update()` each frame from the anchor's world matrix. Evidence: chute logged `Canopy visual attached` yet was never visible after `GetIn ok` (`logs_2026-08-17_22-45-22`); the freefall path already world-drove the same mesh.

- **`SetOrigin` never collides.** A script-flown pawn (AI drop autopilot) crosses walls and then lands on the interior floor, and no landing-time enclosure test can recover it — that trace already starts inside, where an up-trace can leave through the underside of the roof. Sweep the **full 3D step** (`TraceSphere` + `TraceMove` at torso height), slide the blocked remainder along `TraceParam.TraceNorm`, and clamp Y to the first `WORLD | ENTS` shell from well above the pawn (skip trees / small props). A **horizontal-only** chest sweep plus a short down-ray from the feet walks XY under a sloped one-sided face (approach-angle); the ray then starts inside and reports the void floor. Test "is there a roof over me" by tracing *down* from above the point, not up from it. Vanilla placement uses `TraceSphere` and warns that the engine "sometimes lets TraceBoxes travel through terrain". Evidence: `Game/Helpers/SCR_EmptyPositionHelper.c:28-45`; `TraceParam.c` `TraceNorm`; `runtime: user report` airborne QRF through pyramid voids after open-sky LZ + landing relocate; some jumpers landed on the slope, others (shallow heading) ended on the interior floor.

